  + [B1NP-003] require THEBRAIN\enjer as preparation principal and recovery owner and require D:\CantorB1 absent on the named D: NTFS volume before creation
  + [B1NP-004] create only the exact envelope fixture candidate state SQLite canary temporary schema and evidence role paths with the locked containment and separation matrix
  + [B1NP-005] create deterministic nonsecret canaries and one deterministic local disposable Git candidate using the exact selected Git executable with no ambient identity hook remote or user configuration
  + [B1NP-006] rehash immutable inputs before effect and launch the native executable directly with app-server generate-json-schema --out D:\CantorB1\fixture\schema
  + [B1NP-007] schema launch begins with an empty inherited environment and adds only fixed nonsecret required values whose state and temporary paths stay inside the fixture
  + [B1NP-008] bound stdout stderr total bytes elapsed time child and descendant ownership interruption termination wait and late output and require one terminal attempt without executable substitution
  + [B1NP-009] inventory all prepared and generated regular files roots Git identities schema relative paths byte counts and SHA256 while refusing reparse out-of-root drift or unexpected membership
  + [B1NP-010] emit one preparation result whose disposition is Prepared or Quarantined and never represent preparation as a B1 preflight run or sandbox proof
  + [B1NP-011] grant no provider model MCP browser connector network WebSocket thread turn remote download install principal-repository child mutation cleanup deletion retry substitution or recovery execution
  + [B1NP-012] retain every attempted fixture for the named recovery owner and require a second exact final B1 source SJS phase lock and signature before implementation or process launch
